{"date":"2026-02-20","domain":"feature_engineering","type":"bug_fix","severity":"medium","title":"creative_factors.py had wrong 2025-2026 promoted teams (placeholder never updated)","description":"2025-2026 entry was {Bari, Catanzaro, Cesena} (placeholder) instead of {Sassuolo, Pisa, Cremonese} (actual). This meant home_is_promoted, away_is_promoted features were wrong for all 2025-2026 matches, AND the promoted_home/promoted_away betting tags were not applying to actual promoted teams. Affects both feature engineering and situational edge adjustments.","resolution":"Fixed to {Sassuolo, Pisa, Cremonese}. Note: features.parquet needs rebuild to propagate the fix to historical 2025-2026 matches used in training. Current prediction-time features are computed correctly since creative_factors runs at prediction time too.","files":["features/creative_factors.py"],"tags":["promoted_teams","placeholder","creative_factors","feature_engineering","betting_tags"]}{"timestamp": "2026-02-22T15:00:00", "agent": "data-validator", "finding": "feature_selection_fold0_bias", "severity": "warning", "summary": "Walk-forward feature selection runs on fold-0 only (test=2010-2011). 390 features with 98-100% recent coverage are systematically excluded because they have 0% coverage in the 2005-2010 training window used for fold-0. Affected groups: Sofascore rolling (271 cols, 98% recent), FBref rolling (99 cols, 100% recent from 2017), weather (12 cols, 99% recent from 2020). These features never get importance scores and are dropped before any fold sees them. Fix: run feature selection on a recent fold (e.g., 2021+ train set) OR use a time-stratified importance averaging.", "affected_files": ["ml/training.py", "features/build.py"], "command_to_reproduce": "python3 -c \"import pandas as pd; df=pd.read_parquet(\"data/features/features.parquet\"); print(df[df[\"season\"]<\"2022-2022\"][\"home_ss_roll_xg\"].notna().sum())\""}
